esync: send a new event's fd with the create_event reply

With esync, a new event cost three wineserver round trips before its first
wait: create_event, get_inproc_sync_fd for its eventfd, and later close_handle.
WoW creates and closes about 1,000 to 1,300 short-lived events a second on each
of three threads. The server now passes the eventfd along with the
create_event reply, so get_inproc_sync_fd is no longer needed for them.

Changes the server protocol: ntdll and wineserver must come from the same build.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/esync.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/esync.c
index ea7722d..efcab06 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/esync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/esync.c
@@ -385,6 +385,20 @@ static void esync_close_fd_later( int fd )
     if (old >= 0) close( old );
 }
 
+/* Caches the fd the server sent along with the handle of a new object, so the first wait on
+ * it needs no get_inproc_sync_fd request. Caller must hold fd_cache_mutex. */
+void esync_add_new_object( HANDLE handle, int type, int fd, unsigned int shm_idx )
+{
+    if ((fd = esync_move_fd_high( fd )) < 0)
+    {
+        /* Not cached: the first use of the object asks the server for the fd as before. */
+        log_missing_fd( handle, type );
+        return;
+    }
+    /* add_to_list() closes our fd itself when another thread cached the handle first. */
+    if (!add_to_list( handle, type, fd, shm_idx ? get_shm( shm_idx ) : 0 )) close( fd );
+}
+
 NTSTATUS esync_close( HANDLE handle )
 {
     UINT_PTR entry, idx = handle_to_index( handle, &entry );
